Z||000001||mrfiero||07-02-2001||01:53 PM||||I'm not a racer, but I'm in Colorado!  I wish I could make it, but I will be on the road headed east.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Unless you have done some mods to your Fiero, low 15's probably won't happen.  The altitude really slows up a car.  I don't have the exact figures, but I know for each 1000 feet in elevation your times drop by X......I'd say a stock V-6 Fiero will be in the mid to high 16 second range, but I could be wrong. <P>Let us know how you do......I am curious how a Fiero does at altitude too (I have never taken my GT to the track, so I have no idea what it'll do here).||||reg||1
